{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit has a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" that mimics the native iOS keyboard. It can be used for alphabetic, numeric & symbolic keyboards, as well as completely custom ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardLayout","isActive":true},{"text":"s, and supports many different ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Keyboard\/InputType","isActive":true},{"text":"s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"columns":[{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"KeyboardView-English-Callout"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"size":1,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"KeyboardView-Swedish-Theme"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"numberOfColumns":2,"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" will set up most things, like applying gestures, view styles, callouts, etc. based on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardState","isActive":true},{"text":". It automatically observes all observable contexts and can render all ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/Locale\/keyboardKitSupported","isActive":true},{"text":" locales.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" will by default take up as much space as it needs, and resize the keyboard extension frame accordingly. It will also honor settings like ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/isAutoCollapseKeyboardEnabled","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardSettings\/keyboardDockEdge","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext\/isKeyboardFloating","isActive":true},{"text":" etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"👑 KeyboardKit Pro Gold unlocks support for all supported locales and injects an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/EmojiKeyboard"},{"text":" view into the keyboard view.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Tip","style":"tip","type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Customization","anchor":"Customization","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" can be customized in many ways, for instance by changing observable state in the various contexts and settings, by applying various view modifiers and by using the initializer’s view builders to customize the various nested content views.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Behavior","anchor":"Behavior","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The easiest way to customize the keyboard behavior is to inherit ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/StandardKeyboardActionHandler","isActive":true},{"text":" and customize the behavior of any gesture on any action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Actions-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" article for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Layout & Callouts","anchor":"Layout--Callouts","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The easiest way to customize the keyboard layout is to inject a layout in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" initializer. You can use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardLayout\/standard(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" function to get a standard layout for the current context, then modify it if needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The easiest way to customize the secondary callout actions is to apply a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardCalloutActions(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" modifier to the view and customize the standard actions that are provided as view builder parameters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Layout-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Callouts-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" articles for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Views & Styles","anchor":"Views--Styles","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can customize any view or button content in the keyboard, by injecting custom view builders into the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" initializer:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["KeyboardView(","    layout: ...,                        \/\/ You can inject a custom layout if you want to","    services: controller.services,      \/\/ You can inject a controller's or custom services","    buttonContent: { $0.view },         \/\/ You can customize the content view of any button","    buttonView: { $0.view },            \/\/ You can customize the entire view of any button","    collapsedView: { $0.view },         \/\/ You can customize the collapsed keyboard view","    emojiKeyboard: { $0.view },         \/\/ You can customize the emoji keyboard, if any","    toolbar: { params in params.view }  \/\/ You can customize the toolbar above the keyboard",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can return ","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.view","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"params in params.view","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to use the original views, or return any custom view based on the params.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also completely replace the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true},{"text":" with another view at any time. Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardReplacementOverlay(isPresented:content:)","isActive":true},{"text":" extension to replace the keyboard with a custom view of the same size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To customize view styling, just apply the many view modifiers, like ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardViewStyle(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":", or the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardTheme(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" modifier to apply a complete ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardTheme","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Styling-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Themes-Article","isActive":true},{"text":" articles for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Essentials-KeyboardView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"role":"article","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"Feature-Essentials-KeyboardView.jpg"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Essentials - KeyboardView"},"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the essential ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","type":"reference"},{"text":" and how to use and configure it.